-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",97,{
[3073]="700684E6\n1\tSpeak with Harthabor on the outer wall of Jax Phanâl\tHarthabor is pleased with all of the work you've done for the Order of the Eagle. He asks that you speak to him so he can provide details about how you can meet with Achardis.\n2\tYou were told to travel to the Fleet-fast docks and then head east into the Lower Ward to find Achardis's bath-house, located on the northern side of the ward.\t\n",
[3074]="70064F6B\n1\tTalk to Borion north of Lond Cirion\030Talk to Galleth on the beach south of Lond Cirion\030Talk to Gilvenel on the hill east of Lond Cirion\tLady Marra's scouts can be found outside Lond Cirion to the north, east, and south.\n2\tReturn to Lond Cirion to report of your successes\tNow that you have aided the scouts, you should return to Lond Cirion.\n3\tTalk to Caebar in the central yard of Lond Cirion\tCaebar is in the central yard of Lond Cirion. He seems worried about something.\n",
[3075]="70064F77\n1\tTalk to Caebar in the central yard of Lond Cirion and accompany him to the King\tCaebar is in the central yard of Lond Cirion, where he has confided in you that he is worried about the service King Elessar has asked him to provide.\n2\tTalk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion\tLady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.\n3\tTalk to King Elessar in the main hall of Lond Cirion\tKing Elessar is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.\n4\tTalk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion\tLady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.\n",
[3076]="70064F76\n1\tTalk to Queen Arwen in the main hall of Lond Cirion\tQueen Arwen has something she wishes to say to Lady Marra.\n2\tTalk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion\tLady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.\n3\tTalk to Daeram outside the keep of Lond Cirion\tDaeram is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.\n4\tTalk to Orgolas outside the keep of Lond Cirion\tOrgolas is outside the keep of Lond Cirion.\n",
[3077]="700583EE\n1\tTalk to Runerik Knotbeard in Limlók\tRunerik Knotbeard is outside his lodge in the village of Limlók.\n2\tTake some small parchments from the box of scrolls\tThe box of scrolls is near the task board in Limlók.\n3\tFind Glóin and his ravens in the centre of Limlók\tGlóin is in the centre of the village, preparing his ravens to carry messages to Skarháld and the Lonely Mountain.\n4\tBring the small parchments to Glóin in Limlók\tGlóin is in the centre of the village, preparing his ravens to carry messages to Skarháld and the Lonely Mountain.\n5\tTalk to Vídar\tA young Beorning child stands nearby, fascinated by Glóin and the messenger-ravens.\n6\tTalk to Yrsa Spearwife in Limlók\tYrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók. According to her son Vídar, Yrsa has tasked him with scouting outside the village once a week.\n7\tTalk to Vídar at one of his three favourite scouting locations\tYrsa told you to scout the wild lands south of Limlók with her son Vídar. You will find the Beorning boy at one of three different spots: to the south-east, south, or south-west of the village.\n8\tTalk to Yrsa Spearwife in Limlók\tYrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.\n9\tFind the dwarves behind Runerik and Yrsa's lodge\tThe dwarves have gathered behind Runerik and Yrsa's lodge to release the messenger-ravens.\n10\tTalk to Imák behind Runerik's lodge\tImák is behind Runerik's lodge to watch the release of the messenger-ravens.\n11\tWatch the departure of the messenger-ravens\tThe messenger-ravens will bear word of the new Lord of Gundabad to Durin at Skarháld and to King Thorin in the Lonely Mountain.\n12\tTalk to Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge in Limlók\tRunerik Knotbeard is outside his lodge in the village of Limlók.\n",
[3078]="70048C54\n1\tTalk to Ayorzén in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate\tAyorzén the Wily is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n3\tComplete 'Chapter 3.2: The Valley of Webs' in Lhingris\030Complete 'Chapter 3.2: The Second Garrison' in Lhingris\030Complete 'Chapter 3.3: The Gúrzyul' in Talath Úrui\030Complete 'Chapter 3.3: Fate of the Stonemaiden' in Talath Úrui\tMithrandir has asked you to follow both of the leads you have uncovered, accompanying Atli into Lhingris and Harthalín into Talath Úrui.\n4\tTalk to Mithrandir in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n",
[3079]="70064C82\n1\tTalk to Beriaudur by the steps south-east of the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor\tBeriaudur, leader of the city's guard, can be found south-east of the Palace of the Swan, in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.\n2\tFind the guard keeping an eye on Jajax to the east, beyond the market stalls\tA guard keeping watch on Jajax's movements in Dol Amroth is to the east, beyond the market stalls.\n3\tTalk to Tholion by the market stalls\tThe guard Tholion is distressed about something.\n4\tSeek Jajax in the vicinity of Lindor in the courtyard to the north\tTholion sent you to check with Lindor, another of his company, in the courtyard to the north.\n5\tTalk to Lindor in the courtyard\tLindor seems to have also misplaced Jajax.\n6\tFollow the sound of the unusual gull-call down the street to the east\tThe gull-call you heard came from the street to the east and seemed rather out-of-place.\n7\tLook for the source of the strange gull-call\tThe gull-call you heard came from this tree-shaded street and seemed quite out-of-place.\n8\tTalk to Jajax in the tree-shaded street in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor\tJajax stands in a tree-shaded street in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.\n",
[3080]="700583EF\n1\tTalk to Glóin behind Runerik's lodge\tGlóin is behind Runerik's lodge, and from there you heard a great commotion. What has happened?\n2\tUse Injured Hjála\030Use Injured Vaka\tSome of the ravens were shot from the sky by Orc archers! You have to retrieve them from the White Mare and learn if any of Glóin's messages escaped the Floodfells.\n3\tTalk to Venko at the north-western point of the White Mare\tVenko is at the north-western point of the White Mare.\n4\tConfront the unexpected visitors north-west of the White Mare, across the river\tSome unexpected visitors have come north-west of the White Mare, across the river from your dwarf companions. Why have they followed you here?\n5\tTalk to Runerik Knotbeard north-west of the White Mare\tRunerik stands before some of his assembled people north-west of the White Mare, and demands to speak with you.\n6\tCollect flood-broom by rivers in the Floodfells (total: 6)\030Collect unspent arrows from Orcs (total: 3)\tFlood-broom can be found alongside rivers and streams throughout the Floodfells. Runerik also wants his wife Yrsa to examine unspent arrows carried by Orcs in the area, and has asked you to collect some.\n7\tBring the unspent arrows to Yrsa Spearwife in Limlók for her inspection\tYrsa Spearwife is in south-east Limlók.\n8\tTalk to Runerik Knotbeard inside his lodge in Limlók\tRunerik Knotbeard will meet you inside the lodge to treat the injured messenger-ravens.\n9\tAdd the flood-broom to the boiling water in the north room of Runerik's lodge\tRunerik has prepared a pot of boiling water in the north room, and he wants you to add the flood-broom you collected to it.\n10\tWait for the flood-broom tea to properly steep\tThe flood-broom will take some time to steep in the boiling water.\n11\tCollect the flood-broom tea inside Runerik's lodge\tThe flood-broom tea is now prepared, and waits for you to bring it to Runerik.\n12\tBring the flood-broom tea to Runerik Knotbeard inside his lodge\tRunerik is inside his lodge, tending to the wounded messenger-ravens.\n",
[3081]="70064C86\n1\tTalk to Jajax in Dol Amroth and hear his story\tJajax stands on a tree-shaded street in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.\n2\tTalk to Jajax in Dol Amroth, in King's Gondor\tJajax stands on a tree-shaded street in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.\n3\tTalk to Prince Imrahil in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor\tPrince Imrahil is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.\n",
[3082]="70048C56\n1\tFind a message addressed to Ugrukhôr somewhere in Cirith Ungol\tAtli Spider-bane believes that you should enter Cirith Ungol while the Orcs are dealing with the newly-crazed spiders of Lhingris.\n2\tBring the message for Ugrukhôr to Atli Spider-bane outside the Tower of Cirith Ungol (The message can be read from your inventory)\tAtli Spider-bane is not far from the approach to Cirith Ungol, in Lhingris.\n",
[3083]="70048C55\n1\tFind Atli Spider-bane in northern Lhingris, east of the Durthang entrance\tAn entrance to Lhingris can be found in Durthang or by passes in Udûn or Dor Amarth.\n2\tTalk to Atli Spider-bane in northern Lhingris\tAtli Spider-bane is in north-eastern Lhingris, near the pass to Dor Amarth.\n3\tDefeat spiders in Lhingris (total: 12)\tSpiders can be found throughout Lhingris, to Atli's delight.\n4\tTalk to Atli Spider-bane at the approach to Cirith Ungol\tAtli Spider-bane is within view of the the approach to Cirith Ungol.\n5\tExamine the approach to Cirith Ungol\tAtli thought you should more closely inspect the approach to Cirith Ungol.\n6\tAtli thought you should more closely inspect the approach to Cirith Ungol, ensuring that the Orcs that lie in death before the tower are truly slain.\t\n7\tTalk to the mortally-wounded Orc while he yet lives\tOne of the Orcs lying on the approach to Cirith Ungol lived still, but he is close to death. What might he tell you of the situation in Lhingris?\n8\tTalk to Atli Spider-bane at the approach to Cirith Ungol\tAtli Spider-bane is not far from the approach to Cirith Ungol.\n",
[3084]="700583F0\n1\tTalk to Yrsa Spearwife inside her lodge\tYrsa is inside the lodge, waiting to speak with you.\n2\tAppraise Yrsa Spearwife inside the lodge\tYrsa has asked you to try and appraise her skills.\n3\tTalk to Yrsa Spearwife inside her lodge\tYrsa is inside the lodge, waiting to speak with you.\n4\tOnce again appraise Yrsa Spearwife inside the lodge\tPractice makes perfect! Yrsa has asked you to once again try and appraise her skills.\n5\tTalk to Yrsa Spearwife inside her lodge\tYrsa is inside the lodge, waiting to speak with you.\n6\tFind Glóin in Limlók and appraise his skills\tYrsa has asked you to try and appraise Glóin's skills. The old dwarf should be somewhere outside in Limlók.\n7\tTalk to Glóin in Limlók\tGlóin is in Limlók, wondering why you have been studying him so closely.\n8\tFind Imák on the western side of Limlók and appraise his skills\tGlóin wants you to appraise Imák's skills. Imák is on the western side of Limlók.\n9\tTalk to Imák in Limlók\tImák is in Limlók, and he wants to know why you have subjected him to such scrutiny.\n10\tFind Venko by the south-east entrance to Limlók and appraise his skills\tImák wants you to appraise Venko's skills. Venko is by the south-east entrance of Limlók.\n11\tTalk to Venko in Limlók\tVenko is in Limlók, and he is suspicious of the recent attention you have given him.\n12\tAppraise Runerik Knotbeard outside the lodge\tThe real test of your appraisal ability will be to appraise Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge.\n13\tTalk to Runerik Knotbeard outside his lodge in Limlók\tRunerik Knotbeard is outside his lodge and interested to know your appraisal of his skills.\n",
[3085]="70064C85\n1\tTalk to Captain Maeral in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor\tCaptain Maeral is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.\n2\tTalk to Jajax in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor\tJajax is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.\n3\tTalk to Prince Imrahil in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor\tPrince Imrahil is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.\n4\tTalk to King Elessar in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor\tKing Elessar is in the Palace of the Swan, in King's Gondor.\n5\tTalk to Jajax in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor\tJajax is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.\n6\tWait for Jajax to leave\tJajax has decided to leave.\n7\tTalk to Prince Imrahil in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor\tPrince Imrahil is in the Palace of the Swan in Dol Amroth, King's Gondor.\n",
[3086]="70048C57\n1\tTalk to Zaghárog and witness what he wishes to tell you\tThe watching-stone inhabited by Zaghárog stands by the road to Nargroth, on the eastern edge of Talath Úrui.\n2\tTalk to Harthalín by the road to Nargroth\tHarthalín is by the road to Nargroth, on the eastern edge of Talath Úrui.\n",
[3087]="70048C58\n1\tMeet up with Harthalín outside Fushaum Bal, in Talath Úrui\tThe lawless settlement of Fushaum Bal is south-west of Orodruin, in Talath Úrui.\n2\tTalk to Harthalín outside Fushaum Bal\tHarthalín is outside Fushaum Bal, in Talath Úrui.\n3\tEasterlings can be found around Fushaum Bal, in Talath Úrui.\t\n4\tEasterlings can be found around Fushaum Bal, in Talath Úrui.\t\n5\tBring the orders concerning Nargroth to Harthalín outside Fushaum Bal (The orders can be read from your inventory)\tYou found a crumpled parchment on the body of an Easterling in Talath Úrui.\n6\tFind the road that leads to Nargroth, on the eastern side of Talath Úrui\tNargroth, the Caverns of Fire, can be found on the eastern side of Talath Úrui, beyond the Ghâshghurm.\n7\tTalk to the spirit in the stone\tA watching-stone outside the Caverns of Fire has taken an interest in you.\n8\tFind the scorched skull in a cell within the prison of Naerband using the information in your quest journal\tThe spirit in the stone outside Nargroth showed you the location of a scorched skull within a cell in Naerband. If you understood its wish correctly, it has promised to tell you about the Gúrzyul if you return with the skull. You witnessed that Naerband consists of three large chambers, connected by hallways and subdivided by walls and iron bars. The skull is on the floor of a cell in the south-western corner of the largest, northernmost chamber. The iron door to the cell was half-open, and you saw flame-spirits floating over the fog-covered floor.\n9\tBring the scorched skull to the watching-stone outside Nargroth\tA watching-stone outside the Caverns of Fire has taken an interest in you, and awaits delivery of the skull you agreed to bring to it.\n10\tTalk to Harthalín outside Nargroth\tHarthalín is by the watching-stone outside Nargroth, on the eastern side of Talath Úrui.\n",
[3088]="70048C59\n1\tTalk to Ayorzén at Cirith Gorgor, inside the Black Gate\tAyorzén the Wily is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n2\tGain entrance to Agarnaith from the north\030Gain entrance to Agarnaith from the south\tAgarnaith may be approached from either the north or the south.\n3\tYou found adventurers in Agarnaith, and should hear what they have encountered within the Bloody Gore.\t\n4\tDefeat foul creatures in Agarnaith (total: 12)\tThe creatures of Agarnaith seem to draw strength from the foetid air, and you must oppose them for the good of those who adventure in the marsh.\n5\tMeet up with the adventurers near the junction with the eastern road, in Agarnaith\tYou agreed to meet up with the adventurers again on the road, near where the eastern path leads away into the swamp.\n6\tTalk to Linadar on the road in Agarnaith\tOnly Linadar met up with you at the arranged meeting place in Agarnaith.\n7\tSearch for Raneleg to the north, west of the road\030Search for Arodrog just south of the eastern road\030Learn the fate of Raneleg\030Learn if Arodrog is alive or dead\tRaneleg and Arodrog ran into trouble off the road to the north and south, and Linadar has asked you to learn if they yet live.\n8\tBring Raneleg's sword to Linadar in Agarnaith\tLinadar is just north of the junction with the eastern road, in Agarnaith.\n9\tTalk to Mithrandir in Cirith Gorgor, inside the Black Gate\tMithrandir is in Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n",
[3089]="70064D37\n1\tTalk to King Elessar in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor\tKing Elessar is in the Palace of the Swan, King's Gondor.\n2\tDefeat enemies in Lamedon and Blackroot Vale, King's Gondor West (total: 18)\030Travel through Calembel in King's Gondor\030Travel through Lothgobel in King's Gondor\030Travel through Dínadab in King's Gondor\tKing Elessar has given you a choice of road north into the Blackroot Vale: either to fight your way through Tarlang's Crown, or to take the longer, safer road through Lamedon.\n3\tTravel to the base of the Hill of Erech in the Blackroot Vale, King's Gondor\tKing Elessar suggested that you travel to the Hill of Erech in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor.\n4\tTalk to Legolas at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor\tLegolas stands at the base of the Hill of Erech.\n",
[3090]="700583F2\n1\tTalk to Glóin outside the lodge in Limlók\tGlóin is outside the lodge in Limlók.\n2\tMeet up with Imák south of the gorge of Sundergrót\030Defeat goblins at Sundergrót (total: 8)\030Collect discarded weapons at Sundergrót (total: 6)\030Talk to Venko on the grassy slope east of Sundergrót\030Talk to Imák beyond the bridge of Skerabrygg\tSundergrót is far to the west of Limlók, and your companions are interested in testing their skills among its rocky crags.\n3\tTalk to Venko south of the gorge of Sundergrót\tVenko is south of the gorge of Sundergrót, eager to discuss his combat training.\n4\tTalk to Glóin south of the gorge of Sundergrót\tGlóin is at Sundergrót, waiting to discuss your companions' exploits at Sundergrót.\n5\tTalk to Glóin and climb with him to High Sundergrót\tGlóin is interested in climbing to the summit above Sundergrót, and he waits for you to speak with him.\n6\tTalk to Durin along the road between the Wells of Langflood and Elderslade\tYou have travelled with Durin to the road that enters Elderslade, where many of his dwarves have begun to prepare for their war on Gundabad.\n",
[3091]="70064D38\n1\tTalk to Caebar at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor\tCaebar stands at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor.\n2\tTalk to Gimli at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor\tGimli stands at the base of the Hill of Erech, in King's Gondor.\n3\tInconvenience Ruthless Dead in the Blackroot Vale, in King's Gondor (total: 8)\tTheir oaths forever broken, the Ruthless Dead now haunt the Blackroot Vale with renewed hatred for the living. Gimli thinks you should inconvenience them, since he isn't certain they can be slain. Ruthless Dead can be found atop the Hill of Erech at night, and on the road to the Paths of the Dead at any time.\n4\tTalk to Rosfin outside her home in Morlad, in King's Gondor\tRosfin, wife of Duinhir, stands outside their home at the highest point of Morlad, in King's Gondor.\n5\tTalk to Duinhir in Morlad, in King's Gondor\tDuinhir stands by his wife Rosfin in Morlad, in King's Gondor.\n6\tTalk to the surly Morlad resident down the hill to the north\tYou should hear the concerns of the folk of Morlad, in King's Gondor.\n7\tTalk to the angry Morlad resident down the hill to the east\tYou should hear the concerns of the folk of Morlad, in King's Gondor.\n8\tTalk to Caebar south-west of the entrance to Morlad in King's Gondor\tCaebar is south-west of the entrance to Morlad, in King's Gondor.\n9\tFind Legolas and Gimli to the west of Morlad in King's Gondor\tLegolas and Gimli are to the west of the entrance to Morlad, in King's Gondor.\n10\tExamine the arrow embedded in the tree\030Talk to Legolas west of Morlad, in King's Gondor\030Talk to Gimli west of Morlad in King's Gondor\tLegolas and Gimli stand at the ready to the west of Morlad.\n11\tTalk to Duinhir outside his home in Morlad, in King's Gondor\tDuinhir stands outside his home at the highest point of Morlad, in King's Gondor.\n",
[3092]="70048C5A\n1\tTalk to Ayorzén at Cirith Gorgor, inside the Black Gate\tAyorzén is at Cirith Gorgor, just inside the Black Gate.\n2\tTalk to Rathnor the waggon-driver\tThe waggon-driver Rathnor can be found near the Black Gate.\n3\tTalk to Rathnor and travel to the city on his waggon\tThe waggon-driver Rathnor can be found near the Black Gate.\n4\tTalk to Mithrandir in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, south of the entrance\tMithrandir is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, just south of the entrance to the city.\n5\tFind a book about the Great Plague in the Houses of Lore\030Find a scholar with kingsfoil to spare in the Houses of Lore\tA book concerning the Great Plague and a scholar willing to part with kingsfoil must both be found within the Houses of Lore, on the southern side of the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith.\n6\tTalk to Ayorzén on the parapet overlooking the city on the south-eastern side of the Fifth Circle\tAyorzén is on the parapet overlooking the city on the south-eastern side of the Fifth Circle, in Minas Tirith.\n7\tBring the kingsfoil to Mithrandir in the First Circle, south of the entrance to the city\tMithrandir is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, just south of the entrance to the city.\n",
[3093]="700583F3\n1\tEnter the war camp of Annâk-khurfu in one of the old dwarf-keeps\tThe war-camp called Annâk-khurfu is north-west of the bridge between the Wells of Langflood and Elderslade, and serves as a gathering place for the arriving armies of dwarves.\n2\tThe war camp is bustling with dwarves preparing for their upcoming assault on Gundabad. You should speak to the dwarves assembled on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu.\t\n3\tThe war camp is bustling with dwarves preparing for their upcoming assault on Gundabad. You should speak to the dwarves assembled on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\t\n4\tTalk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu\tDurin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu, addressing the assembled force of the dwarves.\n",
[3094]="700583F7\n1\tGreet more arriving dwarves on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu\tDurin has asked you to greet the arriving dwarves on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu.\n2\tTalk to Bósi on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu\tDwarves of the Iron Garrison have come to Elderslade to join the great force preparing for the assault on Gundabad.\n3\tTalk to Bori on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu\tDwarves of the Iron Garrison have come to Elderslade to join the great force preparing for the assault on Gundabad.\n4\tTalk to Bróin on the lower level of Annâk-khurfu\tDwarves of the Iron Garrison have come to Elderslade to join the great force preparing for the assault on Gundabad.\n5\tTalk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu\tDurin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\n6\tAppraise Bósi on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu\tConcerned about the dwarves of the Iron Garrison, Durin wants you to appraise Bósi's mood and skills. Bósi has followed you to the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\n7\tTalk to Bósi on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu\tBósi is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\n8\tAppraise Bori on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu\tConcerned about the dwarves of the Iron Garrison, Durin wants you to appraise Bori's mood and skills. Bori has followed you to the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\n9\tTalk to Bori on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu\tBori is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\n10\tFind Bróin somewhere outside, just north of Annâk-khurfu\tBróin did not follow his cousin upstairs. Where did he go? Bori believes Bróin might be outside, just north of Annâk-khurfu.\n11\tAppraise Bróin outside Annâk-khurfu\tConcerned about the dwarves of the Iron Garrison, Durin wants you to appraise Bróin's mood and skills. Bróin did not follow his cousin upstairs, and now he stands by himself outside Annâk-khurfu.\n12\tTalk to Bróin just north of Annâk-khurfu\tBróin is just north of Annâk-khurfu.\n13\tAgree not to tell anyone of Bróin's worries\tBróin is just north of Annâk-khurfu. Bróin has asked that you agree not to tell Durin about his worries.\n14\tTalk to Durin on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu\tDurin is on the upper level of Annâk-khurfu.\n",
[3095]="70048C5B\n1\tTalk to Harthalín just north of the eastward-running road in Agarnaith and collect samples (0/60)\tHarthalín is north of the eastward-running road in Agarnaith, on the way to Kala-gijak.\n2\tCollect samples from animals in Agarnaith (total: 10)\030Collect samples from plants in Agarnaith (total: 10)\030Collect samples of water in Agarnaith (total: 10)\tMithrandir asked you to collect samples from the plants, animals, and water in Agarnaith in order to determine the progress of Lhaereth's experiments.\n3\tBring the samples to Harthalín by the road in Agarnaith\tHarthalín is by the eastward-running road in Agarnaith.\n4\tExamine the Ghâsh-hai shot by Harthalín in Agarnaith, to the north-east\tHarthalín shot an arrow at an Orc attempting to pass north-east of her location in Agarnaith. She wants you to see if it still lives.\n5\tBring the parchment to Harthalín by the road in Agarnaith (The parchment can be read from your inventory)\tHarthalín is by the eastward-running road in Agarnaith.\n",
[3096]="70064D39\n1\tTravel south of the Blackroot Vale in King's Gondor, and rejoin Elessar on the road to Anfalas\tYou planned to rejoin King Elessar south of the Blackroot Vale in King's Gondor, on the road into Anfalas.\n2\tTalk to King Elessar on the road to Anfalas, in King's Gondor\030Talk to Queen Arwen on the road to Anfalas, in King's Gondor\tKing Elessar is on the road to Anfalas, in King's Gondor.\n3\tTravel to the town of Melgobas, in Anfalas\tThe town of Melgobas is to the west along the coast in Anfalas.\n4\tTalk to Anoradan in Melgobas\tAnoradan is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas, in Anfalas.\n",
[3097]="70064F45\n1\tDefeat lynx near Melgobas (total: 4)\030Defeat Corsairs near Melgobas (total: 6)\tCorsairs and lynx threaten the folk of Anfalas in the vicinity of Melgobas.\n2\tTalk to Anoradan in Melgobas\tAnoradan is in the town of Melgobas.\n3\tTalk to Daeram in Melgobas\tDaeram is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas.\n",
[3098]="70064F52\n1\tSearch along the beach at the bottom of the steps in Melgobas\tDaeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south, down below the fishing village of Melgobas.\n2\tSearch for Orgolas along the beach to the east\tDaeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south of Melgobas.\n3\tSearch for Orgolas further east along the beach\tDaeram asked you to search for Orgolas along the beach to the south.\n4\tTalk to Daeram in Melgobas\tDaeram is in the centre of the fishing village of Melgobas.\n5\tTalk to King Elessar in Melgobas\tKing Elessar stands in Melgobas, considering Orgolas's disappearance.\n6\tMeet up with King Elessar outside Barad Faen, in Anfalas\tBarad Faen is west of Melgobas, in Anfalas.\n7\tTalk to King Elessar outside Barad Faen\tKing Elessar kneels outside Barad Faen, studying the ground. It seems the life of a Ranger can be hard to escape!\n8\tExamine the tracks outside Barad Faen\tKing Elessar has found tracks of some sort outside Barad Faen.\n9\tSearch for Orgolas atop Barad Faen\tTracks indicate Orgolas might have climbed Barad Faen.\n",
[3099]="70064F51\n1\tTalk to King Elessar at Barad Faen\tKing Elessar stands by Orgolas, at Barad Faen.\n2\tTravel to the entrance of Lond Cirion\tLond Cirion is to the west of Barad Faen.\n3\tTalk to Orgolas at the entrance to Lond Cirion\tOrgolas is at the entrance of Lond Cirion, in Anfalas.\n4\tTalk to Daeram at the entrance to Lond Cirion\tDaeram is at the entrance to Lond Cirion, in Anfalas.\n5\tFind the main hall of Lond Cirion\tThe main hall of Lond Cirion is located just inside the entrance to the keep.\n6\tTalk to Marra in the main hall of Lond Cirion\tLady Marra is in the main hall of Lond Cirion.\n7\tFind the Lond Cirion library inside the keep\030Find a guardsman on the bridge north-west of Lond Cirion\030Find Orgolas by the docks of Lond Cirion\030Talk to Coruchon in the library of Lond Cirion\030Talk to Aerhant on the bridge to the north-west of Lond Cirion\030Talk to Orgolas by the docks\tMarra suggested you become familiar with the layout of Lond Cirion and those who reside there.\n8\tTalk to King Elessar in the main hall of Lond Cirion\tKing Elessar is in the main hall of Lond Cirion, speaking with Lady Marra.\n",
[3100]="7004942E\n1\tTalk to Orophin in the Court of Lothlórien\tOrophin will take you from the Lothlórien Court to see Lady Galadriel in her garden.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas wishes to talk with you in the Court of Lothlórien.\n",
[3101]="7001AC57\n1\tDestroy the Gift of Gorothúl in Lumul-nar\tThe entrance to the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar is outside, on Zirakzigil, near the ruined crater where the Balrog lies smouldering. Bróin believes that one of the relics Gorothúl left behind in Moria was given to the merrevail infesting the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar and wants you to destroy it.\n2\tTalk to Bróin in the Peaceful Path\tBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located between Zirakzigil and Durin's Way. You have destroyed the relic Gorothúl gave to the merrevail in Lumul-nar and should return now to Bróin.\n",
[3102]="700266C6\n1\tTalk to Bróin and travel to Mirror Halls of Lumul-nar\tThe entrance to the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar is outside, on Zirakzigil, near the ruined crater where the Balrog lies smouldering. Bróin believes that one of the relics Gorothúl left behind in Moria was given to the merrevail infesting the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar and wants you to destroy it.\n2\tTalk to Bróin in the Peaceful Path\tBróin is in the Peaceful Path, located between Zirakzigil and Durin's Way. You have destroyed the relic Gorothúl gave to the merrevail in Lumul-nar and should return now to Bróin.\n",
[3103]="7000F0F5\n1\tBring Tulk's report to Bósi\tBósi is overseeing some of the waggons along the road through Hollin, south-east from the Hollin Gate and then bending to the north-east. Tulk has given you a report to bring to Bósi, one of the dwarves leading the expedition to Hollin.\n",
[3104]="7005AFF9\n1\tMuster to the Iron-folk at Khur Azan\tThe Iron-folk can be found at Khur Azan. You have returned to Khur Azan and should now muster to the Iron-folk waiting in reserve.\n2\tTalk to Dáin at Khur Azan\tDáin can be found at Khur Azan. After arriving at Khur Azan, you have spotted your friend, Dáin. You should talk to Dáin.\n3\tDefeat Orcs at Kamaz-kala (total: 10)\tKamaz-kala can be found slightly north-west of Khur Azan at Azanulbizar. Lord Grór has asked the Iron-folk to repel the Orcs at Kamaz-kala should the battle need to be joined.\n4\tFind Thromur at Amdân\tThromur can be found at Amdân. After repelling the Orcs at Kamaz-kala, you should find Thromur and investigate what kept him from joining the vanguard.\n5\tAid Thromur\tThromur can be found at Amdân. You have found Thromur and should aid him in completing his errand.\n6\tTalk to Thromur and forge 'Bonds of Oak and Iron'\tThromur can be found at Amdân. You have discovered a likely culprit in the theft of Urro's hand. You should aid Thromur.\n7\tTalk to Dáin at Durin's Stone\tDáin can be found at Durin's Stone. After the defeat of Urro One-hand, the Iron-folk have arrived at Durin's Stone. You should talk to Dáin.\n",
})
